# 1D MOSFET gate stack
# A vertical cut through the channel of an n-channel MOSFET: metal gate, 5 nm SiO2, p-type silicon
# (1e17 cm^-3), the body contact at the bottom. The gate is swept from accumulation through depletion
# into strong inversion; the Device view shows the band bending and the inversion electrons at the
# surface, the Curves tab the gate charge.
#
# The quasi-static solve (equations = equilibrium_poisson): carriers in thermal equilibrium with the
# grounded body and source, as in the channel of a long MOSFET. A 1D cut has no source, so drift-
# diffusion could not supply the inversion layer (ARCHITECTURE.md 6.4).
#
# Mesh (medium): 0.5 nm in the oxide, 1 nm in the first 50 nm of silicon, 10 nm below.

[mesh]
type = tensor
x = linspace(0, 5nm, 11) + linspace(5nm, 55nm, 51) + linspace(55nm, 1um, 95)
straddle x = 5nm 0.2nm

[region silicon]
material = silicon

[region oxide]
material = sio2
box = 0 5nm

[doping]
profile = acceptor constant 1e17

[contact gate]
kind = electrode
patch = x_min
electrode = metal
work_function = 4.1

[contact body]
kind = ohmic
patch = x_max

[solver]
equations = equilibrium_poisson

[sweep]
contact gate = -1.5 : 1.5 : 0.05

[output]
sweep = mosfet_1d.nitsweep
device = mosfet_1d.nitdev
table = mosfet_1d.csv
